# @@name@@

A minimal [zapline](https://github.com/samsamurai301/zapline) app.

```sh
zapline dev          # rebuild and restart on every change
cargo run            # or run it once on http://localhost:8080
cargo test           # in-process tests, no sockets
```

Try it:

```sh
curl localhost:8080/
curl localhost:8080/hello/world
```

## Layout

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `src/lib.rs` | Routes and `app()`, which builds the `App` |
| `src/main.rs` | Serves `app()`; set `ADDR` (or just `PORT`) to change the bind address |
| `tests/api.rs` | Integration tests using `app().test()` |

Need more structure (modules, OpenAPI docs, validation)? Create a project with
`zapline new --template api`, or add pieces here with `zapline generate`.
